…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙâWhen thou takest the sum of the children of Israel after their number, then shall they give every man a ransom for his soul unto the LORD, when thou numberest them; that there be no plague among them, when thou numberest them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊThis they shall give, every one that passeth among them that are numbered, half a shekel after the shekel of the sanctuary: (a shekel is twenty gerahs:) an half shekel shall be the offering of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{Every one that passeth among them that are numbered, from twenty years old and above, shall give an offering unto the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡The rich shall not give more, and the poor shall not give less than half a shekel, when they give an offering unto the LORD, to make an atonement for your souls.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙúAnd thou shalt take the atonement money of the children of Israel, and shalt appoint it for the service of the tabernacle of the congregation; that it may be a memorial unto the children of Israel before the LORD, to make an atonement for your souls.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄThou shalt also make a laver of brass, and his foot also of brass, to wash withal: and thou shalt put it between the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar, and thou shalt put water therein.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEFor Aaron and his sons shall wash their hands and their feet thereat:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂwhen they go into the tabernacle of the congregation, they shall wash with water, that they die not; or when they come near to the altar to minister, to burn offering made by fire unto the LORD:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§so they shall wash their hands and their feet, that they die not: and it shall be a statute for ever to them, even to him and to his seed throughout their generations.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ+Moreover the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊTake thou also unto thee principal spices, of pure myrrh five hundred shekels, and of sweet cinnamon half so much, even two hundred and fifty shekels, and of sweet calamus two hundred and fifty shekels,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_and of cassia five hundred shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary, and of oil olive an hin:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆand thou shalt make it an oil of holy ointment, an ointment compound after the art of the apothecary: it shall be an holy anointing oil.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd thou shalt anoint the tabernacle of the congregation therewith, and the ark of the testimony,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaand the table and all his vessels, and the candlestick and his vessels, and the altar of incense,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQand the altar of burnt offering with all his vessels, and the laver and his foot.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd thou shalt sanctify them, that they may be most holy: whatsoever toucheth them shall be holy.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuAnd thou shalt anoint Aaron and his sons, and consecrate them, that they may minister unto me in the priest's office.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel, saying, This shall be an holy anointing oil unto me throughout your generations.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™Upon man's flesh shall it not be poured, neither shall ye make any other like it, after the composition of it: it is holy, and it shall be holy unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyWhosoever compoundeth any like it, or whosoever putteth any of it upon a stranger, shall even be cut off from his people.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book§chapter«first_verse"ªlast_verse&¦verses•„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­And the LORD said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqand thou shalt make it a perfume, a confection after the art of the apothecary, tempered together, pure and holy:¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ±and thou shalt beat some of it very small, and put of it before the testimony in the tabernacle of the congregation, where I will meet with thee: it shall be unto you most holy.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd as for the perfume which thou shalt make, ye shall not make to yourselves according to the composition thereof: it shall be unto thee holy for the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]Whosoever shall make like unto that, to smell thereto, shall even be cut off from his people.¦layout ªlast_verse&